WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.425
In this video, you will learn how to put money into the app, and how to take it back out.

00:00:05.425 --> 00:00:07.420
You need a wallet in the app first.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.899
If you do not have one yet, watch the Start here video first.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.225
Start on the Hub, the home screen with the big tiles.

00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:16.559
Click Wallet Utilities.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.587
Now click Sol Wallet, in the menu on the left.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.699
This is your Solana trading wallet.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:25.831
Scroll down to Deposit address.

00:00:25.831 --> 00:00:29.531
This long line of letters and numbers is your wallet address.

00:00:29.531 --> 00:00:31.897
Think of it like a bank account number.

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:35.052
Click the small copy button on the right to copy it.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.865
Now go to wherever your money is right now.

00:00:38.865 --> 00:00:43.576
That could be an exchange, like Coinbase or Binance, or a wallet, like Phantom.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.067
Choose Withdraw, or Send.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:47.334
Pick SOL, and pick the Solana network.

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:49.361
Paste the address you just copied.

00:00:49.361 --> 00:00:52.284
Send a small amount first, like a tenth of a SOL.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.256
The money usually shows up in less than a minute.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:58.760
Click Refresh, and your balance here goes up.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:00.998
Be careful here.

00:01:00.998 --> 00:01:04.334
Only send SOL, on the Solana network, to this address.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:08.843
A coin sent from a different network, like Ethereum, can be lost forever.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.442
Now, taking money out.

00:01:11.442 --> 00:01:14.330
First, tell the app where your money should go.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:15.805
Find Withdrawal address.

00:01:15.805 --> 00:01:19.676
Paste the address of your own wallet, or your exchange account.

00:01:19.676 --> 00:01:20.659
Then click Save.

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:21.581
Check it twice.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:24.469
Money sent to a wrong address cannot come back.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.885
Next, find Withdraw SOL, just below.

00:01:27.885 --> 00:01:32.397
Type how much SOL you want to take out, or click Max to take out all of it.

00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:35.524
Max leaves a tiny bit behind to pay the network fee.

00:01:35.524 --> 00:01:37.509
Then click Withdraw, and confirm.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.307
There is also a Send box.

00:01:40.307 --> 00:01:44.204
It sends SOL, or any coin you hold, to any address you type in.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.483
You confirm in a pop-up window before anything moves.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.915
Trading on BNB Chain, or Robinhood?

00:01:50.915 --> 00:01:56.782
They each have their own wallet page, in the menu on the left, with their own deposit address.

00:01:56.782 --> 00:02:00.839
To take money out on those chains, use the Send box on that page.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:02.757
That is it.

00:02:02.757 --> 00:02:06.028
To put money in, copy your address and send SOL to it.

00:02:06.028 --> 00:02:09.785
To take money out, save your own address, then click Withdraw.

00:02:09.785 --> 00:02:12.330
And always send a small test amount first.
